STATE

  Version 0.2.4 on branch dev, accepted by Fred on 2026-11-23 after his
  nested sandbox/demo-0.2.4 check (W29). Phase P3 / R1 finding 15: replaces eager
  tp_arrange() / tp_arrange_all() with a per-monitor arrange_dirty flag
  (plus arrange_count) and a single server-owned Wayland idle source
  (tp_server.arrange_idle) that coalesces multiple mutations into one
  arrange pass per dirty monitor per idle, runs tp_idle_update_inhibit()
  and tp_pointer_refocus_now() once per batch, and uses a 64-entry stack
  buffer in sync_tree() to avoid per-arrange heap allocation. Synchronous
  readers (tiled swap/move/resize/drag-begin, popup unconstrain, IPC
  windows/focused, and window events with active listeners) flush on
  demand via tp_arrange_flush().
